# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hugging Face Space → Settings → "Variables and secrets"
# Add each of these as a *Secret* (not a public Variable) for the 24/7 live setup.
# Everything has a safe default in the Dockerfile; you only NEED the ones marked ★.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ★ Sign JWTs with your own key (≥32 chars). Without this, sessions reset on every
#   rebuild and are guessable.
SECRET_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-32+char-string

# ★ Persist data across restarts. Free HF Spaces have NO persistent disk, so the
#   default SQLite DB is wiped on every restart/rebuild. Point at a free managed
#   Postgres (Neon / Supabase / Render) so plates, visits and analytics survive.
#   Format: postgresql+psycopg2://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DBNAME
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://user:pass@host:5432/cartrack

# ★ The camera feed HF will run ANPR on, 24/7. HF cannot reach a LAN camera or the
#   Dahua Easy4IP P2P (UDP) tunnel, so this MUST be an internet-reachable stream:
#     • a cloud relay's view URL (an on-site device pushes the camera to a small
#       VPS running MediaMTX — see deploy/relay/), or
#     • a public RTSP-over-TCP camera (port-forwarded), or
#     • an HLS (.m3u8) URL.
#   Use rtsp://...?rtsp_transport=tcp form when possible (HF blocks RTSP-over-UDP).
LIVE_RTSP_URL=rtsp://your-relay-host:8554/site/cam1
LIVE_RTSP_NAME=Front Gate
# Speed calibration: metres per pixel of motion (0 = engine default). Set from a
# known reference (lane width) for accurate km/h.
LIVE_RTSP_METER_PER_PIXEL=0.0

# ── Optional tuning (defaults already set in the Dockerfile) ──────────────────
# LIVE_24_7_ENABLED=true            # run the supervisor + auto-start cameras on boot
# LIVE_RESUME_ON_STARTUP=true       # bring ANPR back automatically after a restart
# LIVE_SEGMENT_MAX_GB=2             # cap on-disk recordings (no persistent disk on free)
# ANALYSIS_MEDIA_RETENTION_HOURS=6  # auto-delete old MP4s (data is kept in the DB)
# PLATE_JURISDICTION=qa_uk          # qa | uk | qa_uk | intl
